      "full_prompt_override": "Use case: identity-preserve. Create a clean staging atlas of SIXTEEN small animation cutouts for later deterministic packing into a portrait game sheet.\nIDENTITY REFERENCE: Stand.png. Preserve the exact GreenSummon, green/gold jade-mask envoy, pale blue-gray skin, red eyes, jade headband, gold cloud-trimmed robe/armor and long pale-green sashes, LEFT-facing three-quarter angle. Preserve exact complete tall green banner: full dark-green pole with gold bands, jade diamond finials at BOTH ends, gold crossbar, two jade bead green tassels, large emerald swallowtail cloth with gold border and gold/light-green cloud pattern. Anatomical left hand at image right holds the pole, anatomical right hand at image left remains open. Same detailed clean cel-shaded line art and palette.\nLAYOUT FOR THIS STAGING IMAGE: SQUARE 1024x1024 transparent PNG. Exactly 4 columns x 4 rows, 16 invisible 256x256 SQUARE cells. Each entire character AND banner are SMALL, about 150px wide x 190px tall, centered inside the square cell. At least 40px transparent empty LEFT AND RIGHT margins and 30px TOP AND BOTTOM margins in every square cell. VERY WIDE transparent gutters. Leave plenty of empty space. Do NOT fill the square cells. Do NOT let flags, fingers, boots, sashes, finials or tassels touch another sprite, overlap or touch canvas edges. Exactly one complete envoy and one complete banner per cell. Identical small fixed drawing scale, soles on consistent cell-local y=226.\nThe background and gutters must be real empty alpha zero. No opaque background, scenery, gradients, floor or shadows. No grid, text, labels, numbers, borders or effects.\nAnimation: IDLE breathing loop, 16 sequential frames. F1 neutral with both boots planted, left hand holding the VERTICAL banner and right hand open; F2-5 chest rises and banner cloth lifts/ripples, jade tassels sway; F6-9 slow exhale, open casting hand turns slightly and robe hem drifts; F10-13 cloth settles and tassels sway back; F14-16 return exactly to F1. Keep pole shaft upright/vertical and boot positions fixed throughout; only tiny breathing and cloth movement. No stepping or casting effects. Preserve identical banner silhouette design and cloth pattern as it ripples.\nSixteen sequential breathing poses left-to-right top-to-bottom, gentle chest motion, cloth and tassel sways, feet planted, pole upright; all body parts and all banner parts fully visible and separated.",
